NAME
       monitor - graphical system monitor

SYNOPSIS
       monitor

DESCRIPTION
       Shows CPU, memory, swap, network, disk and process information read
       from /proc. Tabs: Overview, Processes, Resources, Network, Disks and
       Settings. Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+6 switch tabs, Ctrl+Q closes the window.

       The Processes tab lists PID, name, user, state, CPU share, resident
       memory and thread count. Click a column header to sort, type in the
       filter box to narrow the list, select a row and use End process
       (SIGTERM) or Kill (SIGKILL). Both ask for confirmation. Processes
       owned by root are marked with a lock; their buttons are disabled
       unless the monitor runs as root. The kernel enforces the same rule:
       a user may only signal processes of the same uid, root may signal any.
       CPU share is the part of the total processor capacity used.

FILES
       ~/.config/monitor/monitor.conf
              Settings, one "key = value" per line.
       /usr/share/monitor/themes/NAME.theme
              Built-in themes.
       ~/.config/monitor/themes/NAME.theme
              User themes. A name already taken by an earlier theme is
              ignored.

SETTINGS
       theme                  theme name
       interval_ms            update interval, 250 to 5000
       history                samples kept in graphs, 30 to 600
       start_tab              overview, processes, resources, network,
                              disks or settings
       show_system_processes  true or false
       sort_column            pid, name, user, state, cpu, memory, threads
       sort_order             asc or desc
       cpu_view               cores or combined
       units                  auto, kib or mib
       smooth                 true or false

THEME FORMAT
       Lines of the form "key = value". Colors are written #rrggbb. Empty
       lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Missing keys take the
       values of the Default theme.

       name     theme name
       light    true or false; picks a matching light or dark toolkit style
                for buttons and menus

       Colors: background, surface, surface2, border, foreground,
       foreground_dim, accent, selection, selection_text, warning, danger,
       success.

       Graph gradients, each with the suffixes _low, _mid and _high: cpu,
       mem, download, upload (for example cpu_low, cpu_mid, cpu_high).

SEE ALSO
       ps(1), free(1), kill(1)
